Primary Goal: PRIMARY-GOAL-260728-3lhfz3 revision 1
State: active
Objective: Deliver a working, signed and notarized macOS-first Relux Tunnel client that presents as a full-tunnel NEPacketTunnelProvider VPN and uses authenticated SSH with libssh2 as the primary external transport to a user-controlled host. Complete all gate-free SPM core, packet bridge/HEV, SSH viability, TCP/DNS runtime, rootless exec/stdio relay, UDP/degraded mode, macOS UI/provider, self-update, threat-model, CI, signing and release work through tracked producer-reviewer-rework-accepted cycles. iOS, App Store A0 policy research, and native Linux runner evidence are deferred and must not block the macOS prototype. Preserve host-key verification before auth, Keychain-only secret custody, bounded memory, fail-closed DNS, no user-exposed SOCKS, no SFTP, no utun-FD discovery, injectable physical tuning, and stop at real Keychain/Apple provisioning/system-VPN/physical validation/notary or product-decision gates with exact evidence. Execute serially with Codex Sol high as primary orchestrator, Claude Opus 5 as producer, Codex Sol high as independent reviewer, max_parallel 1, lite context, and signed pushed synchronized commits after every accepted task.
